  "subdivision_of_building": "Unit 9:\nAdditional 1 Bed/2 Person \nKitchen, living, dining space relocated to second floor\nStaircase added  to provide access to second floor\n\nUnit 10:\nAdditional 1 Bed/2 Person \nKitchen, living, dining space relocated to second floor\nStaircase added  to provide access to second floor\n\nUnit 11:\nAdditional 1 Bed/2 Person \nKitchen, living, dining space relocated to second floor\nStaircase added  to provide access to second floor\n\nUnit 12: \nAdditional 2no. 1 Bed 2 Person rooms\nKitchen, living, dining space relocated to second floor\nStaircase added  to provide access to second floor\n\nUnit 13: \nIncreased usable floor area at the second floor\nReconfigured layout",
  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "Upwards roof extension of the existing residential development at Pamer Court, alterations to the existing first floor to facilitate the additional area within the second floor in the roof space, additional dormers, the addition of Solar PVs and sufficient amenity provision. ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [24/16/01, 24/16/02, 24/16/03, 24/16/04, 24/16/05, 24/16/06, 24/16/07, 24-16-22, 24-16-23, 3D views, Fire statement, application form- Received 31/03/2026; 24-16-21A , Design and Access Statement (Rev A)- Received 20/04/2026; 24/16/20B- Received 13/05/2026].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - No additional windows or openings shall be formed in the elevations of the development hereby permitted.\r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Secure covered cycle parking facilities (for not less than 28 bicycles) for the occupants of, and visitors to (for not less than two bicycles), the development shall be installed as per dwg no. 24/16/20B. The approved facilities shall conform to the current Westtrans West London Cycle Parking Guidance (or such other guidance as shall supersede it) in design and layout and be fully implemented and made available for use before the first occupation of the development or commencement of the approved use as appropriate and thereafter retained for use at all times without obstruction. \r\nReason: In order to support sustainable transport objectives",
    "Condition : 6 - All refuse and recycling bins or any other items linked to deliveries and collection in association with the approved development are to be stored within the designated areas of the building at all times and only brought out onto the public highway at the time of collection.\r\nReason: To protect the quality of the local environment and to prevent obstruction and inconvenience to users of the public highway.",
    "Condition : 7 - No solar panels shall be installed until a glint and glare assessment has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. No subsequent alterations to the approved scheme are to take place unless submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\nReason: To ensure the development does not endanger the safe movement of aircraft or the operation of Heathrow Airport. The airport requires a glint and glare assessment to be completed to determine the full impact on Air Traffic Control Tower and pilots approaching the airport.\r\n"
  ],
